## Hard rules
1. STACK FREEZE. Astro static on Cloudflare Pages, existing Tailwind setup kept
   exactly as it is. No second styling system, CSS framework, component library,
   React/Vue/Svelte, new fonts, icon library, client router or animation library.
   Do not change the Tailwind config or version, do not bump a dependency to a
   new major, and never rewrite the dependency tree.
2. ZERO-BUNDLE RULE. No new client JavaScript unless a phase names it (max 3 KB,
   deferred). If a fix seems to need a library, stop and tell me.
3. PAYLOAD BUDGET. Homepage under 40 KB transfer, every other page under 22 KB,
   no page gains more than 5 KB, requests per page at or below 6, CLS stays 0,
   LCP under 250 ms. Phase 10 may add exactly one cached CSS request if the page
   total still goes down.
4. PRESERVE EXACTLY: converter output (ITU table, unsupported-character flagging,
   word gaps); one H1 per page; unique title/description/self-canonical per page;
   existing JSON-LD except where a phase names it; /_astro/ assets at immutable
   max-age=31536000; dark mode; contrast (about 15:1, #14110e on #f5efe6); every
   existing paragraph of body copy; the rendered appearance of every page; AND
   the homepage's eager-loaded translator script, byte-for-byte: raw 19,690
   bytes, gzip-9 6,083 bytes, 1 request, hash BFwF2DBv. Re-verify this exact
   hash and both byte counts after every phase that touches astro.config.ts,
   the build pipeline, or any shared/global file - not only Phase 10. If the
   hash changes for any reason, stop and report before continuing, even if the
   byte counts look unchanged.
5. NEVER: rename a URL slug, delete a section, change robots.txt or the sitemap
   index, change the build output directory, reformat whole files, or rewrite
   copy nobody asked for.
6. EDIT STYLE. Surgical, additive edits only. If you must touch a file the phase
   did not name, stop and explain why.
7. CSP STAYS STRICT. public/_headers sends connect-src 'self' and
   script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'. Add only hostnames you watched succeed in
   the browser Network tab. Never wildcards, never 'unsafe-eval'.
8. ACCESSIBILITY FLOOR. No removed focus outlines, no tap targets under 44 px,
   no lost alt text or aria labels.
9. STATUS AND SCHEMA FREEZE. No route's status changes except the one Phase 3
   names. No JSON-LD added or removed except where a phase names it - FAQPage
   stays exactly where it is.
10. FIND, DO NOT GUESS. When a phase names a setting, a line of copy or an email
    address, locate it with grep in the current repo before editing and quote the
    path and line you found. If you cannot find it, say so - do not invent it.
11. TRUST THE MEASUREMENT, NOT THE OLD AUDIT. Four findings from the earlier audit
    do not reproduce and are closed: <th> scope (all present), orphan pages
    (none: 14 pages have 17 inbound links), the speed page's keyword (present),
